<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Saskatchewan River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a> River is formed in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a> by the meeting of the Bow and Oldman rivers and flows through Saskatchewan, past Saskatoon, to join the North Saskatchewan east of Prince Albert. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> families settled river lots along its banks around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batoche">Batoche</a> and St. Laurent in the 1870s, and the fighting of 1885 took place in its valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-saskatchewan-river.jpg" alt="South Saskatchewan River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph by Dean Shareski (https://www.flickr.com/people/shareski/) · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Saskatchewan_River.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
